    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d91">

                <pb facs="0230" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 296/384: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-29T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1924—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>207. L–92, for Logan. Referring to last paragraph your L–179, June 25, 7 p.m.,
                    Owen Young has cabled to Kindersley<anchor n="35" xml:id="d91-f1"/> as
                        follows:<anchor n="36" xml:id="d91-f2"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Hope my suggestion of selecting all personnel at one time after plan is
                            accepted may be adopted and I will come over if that will help. Most
                            important that name should emerge from discussions between Germans,
                            French, English and other allies as their unanimous choice. If you agree
                            can you see that Paris and Berlin avoid personnel discussion for the
                            present. Please answer fully. Young.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d91-f1" n="35" xml:id="d91-f1-content">
                <p>Sir Robert Molesworth Kindersley, British member of the first committee of
                    experts.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d91-f2" n="36" xml:id="d91-f2-content">
                <p>Quotation not paraphrased.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
